{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Vanessa Makes a New Friend"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "What Were You Doing?"}, {"type": "position", "content": 10}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 6}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Describe characteristics of different people and their jobs."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. "}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn5le06ob10re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " The Past Continuous Tense"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You use the Past Continuous tense to talk about something that was happening at a particular time in the past."}, {"type": "text", "content": "This is how you form the Past Continuous tense:<br /><br />  subject + was/were + v-ing<br /> I was cooking.<br /> It was raining."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You often use the Past Continuous tense together with the Simple Past tense.<br /> The Past Continuous talks about a longer \u2018background' action. The Simple Past talks about talks about a shorter event that happened in the middle of, or interrupted, the longer event."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the words <span class =\"strong\">when</span> and <span class =\"strong\">while</span> before the longer action."}, {"type": "example", "content": "While we were eating, a rainbow appeared over the horizon. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "When we got home, it was raining."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to go on a date"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to spend time with someone who you are romantically interested in "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I went on a date today."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le06ob10aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about what you were doing."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Comparative and Superlative Adjectives"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "We use comparatives to compare people and things with other people and things.<br/> Comparative adjectives are forms like <span class=\"italic\">taller</span>, <span class=\"italic\">more attractive</span>.<br/> You use <span class=\"strong\">than</span> after comparatives <br/><br/> We use superlatives to compare people and things with all of the group that they are in. <br/> Superlative adjectives are forms like <span class=\"italic\">the tallest</span>, <span class=\"italic\">the most attractive</span>.<br/> You add <span class=\"strong\">the</span> in front of the superlative form to describe people, places and things."}, {"type": "text", "content": " Look at the chart for information on how to form the comparative and superlative:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"strong\\\">Adjective</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"strong\\\">Comparative</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"strong\\\">Superlative</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"strong\\\">Form</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" tall\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" taller (than) \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"the tallest\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Most adjectives: +er, +-est \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"late   \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"later (than)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"the latest\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adjectives ending in -e: +r, +-st \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"happy\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"happier (than)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"the happiest\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"2-syllable adjectives ending in -y: +ier, +iest\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"attractive\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"more attractive (than) \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"the most attractive \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"3+-syllable adjectives:  more + adjective+ than  most + adjective \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"good<br /> bad\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"better (than)<br /> worse (than)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"the best<br /> the worst\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Irregular comparisons\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "He's more considerate than other guys. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "It was the most incredible moment!"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "rainbow"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "different colors in the sky caused by light going through water "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: A rainbow appeared in the sky."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le06ob10aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "horizon"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "in the distance, where the sky meets the land "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: A rainbow appeared on the horizon."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le06ob10aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "considerate"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "polite"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He is very considerate."}, {"type": "audio",